 <p><strong>What&#8217;s the difference between Zone A, AE, and AO?</strong><br />
-They&#8217;re all high-risk zones where your lender requires insurance. Zone AE is the most common (elevation-determined); AO is shallow flooding (usually 1-3 feet). Prices are similar, though Zone AH (shallow flooding with known depth) runs about $75 higher. The zone matters for the lender requirement, but Risk Rating 2.0 prices your actual building risk, not just the zone letter.</p>
